# Aloe: a clump of LONG, thick, fleshy, green-grey leaves rising from the ground and curving UP (`Cup`, `UpAttract`), not
# fanning out, flecked with pale spots in bands (~0.8-1.2 m tall). It grows ON ITS OWN on hot, dry ground - the desert
# and its dry edges (its Placement block: no tree needed); Climate Desert - no tree's - so it is never a tree's
# undergrowth.
# The leaves are the modules: one thick blade each (`Section`: a shallow gutter on top; `Swell`; `Tip`), no leaf cards;
# the spots are the bark's dashes. The crown starts above the ground on a short hidden trunk.
TreeSpecies Aloe
	Kind Bush
	Climate Desert
	Seed 157
	Scale 1.0 1.5
	Wind
		Trunk 0
		Branch 0.1
	Trunk
		Count 2
		Height 0.2 0.3
		Radius 0.07
		Taper 0.7
		Flare 0
		Sink 0.1
		Curve 2
		Rings 3
		Sides 8
	Crown
		Shape Cone
		Start 0.3
		Radius 0.55
		Slots 17
		Fill 1
		Angle 42 15
		AngleVar 6
		BranchRadius 3
	# 3 leaf modules (3 widths, `Section` widthVar): each one is a billboard bake and a row of the card atlas.
	Module
		Count 3
		Radius 0.07
		Curve 8 4
		UpAttract 0.5
		Cup 25
		Rings 14
		Sides 12
		Section 1.2 0.5 0.35 0.25
		Swell 0.4
		Tip 0.35
	Leaves
		Type Single
		PerBranch 0
	# Two baked plants are enough (they look alike): half the billboard textures.
	Bake
		Variants 2
	Billboard
		Distance 25
		Resolution 256
		FadeWidth 6
	Bark
		Plates 8 1
		Crack 0.03
		Breakup 0.95
		Relief 0.2
		Lichen 0
		Lenticels 0.5
		LenticelSize 1.5
	Color
		Bark 0.38 0.50 0.34
		Leaf 0.38 0.50 0.34
		Mark 0.72 0.78 0.64
	Placement
		Density 20
		Temperature 18 1000
		Precipitation 50 400
		ClimateWidth 0.02
		Cluster 40 0.5
		MaxSlope 0.9
